P-MARBLE

Production-Grade Evidence-Centric Retrieval & Decision Support Engine

Overview

P-MARBLE is a production-grade, evidence-centric retrieval and synthesis system designed for high-stakes, real-world decision support. It integrates multimodal evidence, hybrid retrieval, and deterministic consistency checks into a guarded synthesis pipeline that prioritizes auditability, reproducibility, and safety over speculative reasoning.

P-MARBLE is explicitly not an autonomous reasoning or forecasting system.
It is a conservative decision-support engine that surfaces what is known, what is disputed, and what is missing, with strict provenance guarantees.

Design Goals

P-MARBLE is built around the following non-negotiable principles:

Evidence before inference
No claim is surfaced without traceable source evidence.

Explicit uncertainty
The system must refuse synthesis when confidence thresholds are not met.

Bounded automation
Agentic behavior is constrained, deterministic, and observable.

Audit-grade reproducibility
Every run is replayable with immutable inputs, configs, and index snapshots.

Production safety
The system prefers refusal over confident error.

What P-MARBLE Is (and Is Not)
P-MARBLE IS

A multimodal evidence ingestion and integration engine

A hybrid retrieval system (lexical, dense, graph)

A conflict-aware claim and timeline builder

A guarded synthesis engine for analyst support

A compliance-friendly, auditable platform

P-MARBLE IS NOT

An autonomous decision maker

A probabilistic forecasting engine

A black-box “reasoning LLM”

A self-modifying agent system

