README for R-MARBLE (research engine)

Below is a clean, external-facing README for R-MARBLE, written as a research-engine document, clearly separated from production, with explicit caveats and scope.
It is intentionally precise, academic in tone, and suitable for internal research teams, labs, or advanced enterprise R&D, not customers.

R-MARBLE

Research-Grade Modular Reasoning & Retrieval Engine

Overview

R-MARBLE is a research-grade retrieval, integration, and reasoning engine designed to explore advanced knowledge-centric AI architectures. It supports probabilistic reasoning, constraint solving, and agentic workflows over multimodal evidence, with an emphasis on reproducibility, experimentation, and interpretability.

R-MARBLE is explicitly not production-safe and is not intended for autonomous or decision-critical deployment. It exists to develop, test, and validate reasoning methods that may later be distilled into conservative, production-safe heuristics.

Research Objectives

R-MARBLE is designed to answer research questions such as:

How can heterogeneous evidence be integrated into coherent explanations?

How do deterministic constraints interact with probabilistic causal models?

When does hybrid retrieval (lexical + dense + graph) improve reasoning quality?

How can uncertainty, contradiction, and missing information be modeled explicitly?

How do bounded agentic workflows compare to free-form multi-agent systems?

Key Research Principles

Explicit reasoning over opaque generation
Reasoning artifacts (constraints, graphs, probabilities) are first-class outputs.

Experimentation over safety
R-MARBLE prioritizes exploration and insight, not operational risk minimization.

Full observability
Every intermediate state is persisted for inspection and ablation.

Reproducibility
All runs are replayable with pinned configs, models, and data snapshots.

What R-MARBLE Is (and Is Not)
R-MARBLE IS

A modular RAG research platform

A testbed for hybrid reasoning (symbolic + probabilistic)

A framework for evaluating retrieval and integration strategies

A sandbox for agentic planning and iterative retrieval

A generator of explainable reasoning artifacts

R-MARBLE IS NOT

A production inference system

A compliance-ready decision engine

A calibrated forecasting system

A user-facing product

