Adjust per-channel budgets

Study retrieval drift and error propagation

Knowledge Integration Research

Integration is treated as a research problem, not a fixed pipeline.

Supported experiments include:

Claim clustering strategies

Conflict resolution heuristics

Temporal alignment methods

Entity resolution algorithms

Schema-induced extraction bias

All integration artifacts are persisted for offline analysis.

Hybrid Reasoning Layer
Deterministic Reasoning (Z3)

R-MARBLE supports general constraint solving, including:

Temporal consistency

Resource and exclusivity constraints

Accounting and identity constraints

Cross-entity logical relationships

Constraints may be:

Hard or soft

Local or global

Experimental or domain-derived

Unsatisfiable cores are retained for study.

Probabilistic Reasoning (Bayesian Networks)

R-MARBLE supports Bayesian Network experimentation using templated causal structures:

Structure learning vs fixed templates

CPD prior sensitivity

Evidence reliability weighting

Posterior explainability and sensitivity analysis

Numeric posteriors are research artifacts only.

Agentic Planning & Iterative Retrieval

R-MARBLE supports bounded agentic workflows via stateful orchestration:

Task decomposition

Iterative retrieval loops

Targeted follow-up queries

Hypothesis-driven evidence acquisition

Budgets and iteration limits are configurable but flexible.

Domain Packs (Research Mode)

Domain Packs in R-MARBLE are experimental modules, not contracts.

They may include:

Ontologies and schemas

Retrieval heuristics

Constraint templates

Bayesian Network structures

Prompt variants

Schema evolution and breaking changes are allowed.

Evaluation & Analysis

R-MARBLE emphasizes offline evaluation:

Retrieval metrics (Recall@k, nDCG)

Citation accuracy

Conflict rates

Constraint violation frequency

BN calibration metrics (e.g., Brier score)

Ablation and sensitivity studies

No single metric is treated as authoritative.

