OpenAPI spec for P-MARBLE 

Below is a production-grade OpenAPI 3.1 specification for P-MARBLE.
It is explicitly conservative, refusal-capable, and audit-first.
This spec assumes batch + async execution with immutable runs and no silent mutation.

The API is intentionally narrow: P-MARBLE is a decision-support engine, not a chat system.

P-MARBLE OpenAPI Specification (v1)
openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: P-MARBLE API
  version: 1.0.0
  description: |
    P-MARBLE is a production-grade, evidence-centric retrieval and decision
    support engine. The API supports immutable, auditable runs with strict
    provenance, trust gating, and refusal semantics.

servers:
  - url: https://api.p-marble.internal/v1

security:
  - bearerAuth: []

tags:
  - name: Runs
  - name: Evidence
  - name: Results
  - name: Admin

paths:

  /runs:
    post:
      tags: [Runs]
      summary: Create a new production run
      description: |
        Initializes an immutable P-MARBLE run with locked configuration,
        schema versions, and retrieval snapshots.
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: "#/components/schemas/RunCreateRequest"
      responses:
        "201":
          description: Run created
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Run"
        "400":
          description: Invalid configuration
        "403":
          description: Unauthorized domain pack or risk class

    get:
      tags: [Runs]
      summary: List runs
      parameters:
        - in: query
          name: status
          schema:
            type: string
            enum: [PENDING, RUNNING, COMPLETED, REFUSED, FAILED]
      responses:
        "200":
          description: List of runs
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: array
                items:
                  $ref: "#/components/schemas/Run"

  /runs/{run_id}:
    get:
      tags: [Runs]
      summary: Get run metadata
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Run metadata
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/Run"

  /runs/{run_id}/execute:
    post:
      tags: [Runs]
      summary: Execute a run
      description: |
        Starts execution of a previously created run.
        Execution is asynchronous.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "202":
          description: Execution started
        "409":
          description: Run already executed or immutable

  /runs/{run_id}/status:
    get:
      tags: [Runs]
      summary: Get run execution status
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Run status
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/RunStatus"

  /runs/{run_id}/result:
    get:
      tags: [Results]
      summary: Get final run result
      description: |
        Returns synthesis output OR explicit refusal with reasons.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Run result
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/RunResult"
        "404":
          description: Result not available

  /runs/{run_id}/evidence:
    get:
      tags: [Evidence]
      summary: List evidence objects used in a run
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Evidence objects
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: array
                items:
                  $ref: "#/components/schemas/EvidenceObject"

  /runs/{run_id}/artifacts:
    get:
      tags: [Results]
      summary: Get run artifacts
      description: |
        Returns references to all persisted artifacts:
        retrieval plans, conflict sets, constraints, and logs.
      parameters:
        - $ref: "#/components/parameters/RunId"
      responses:
        "200":
          description: Artifact manifest
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: "#/components/schemas/ArtifactManifest"

components:

  securitySchemes:
    bearerAuth:
      type: http
      scheme: bearer

  parameters:
    RunId:
      name: run_id
      in: path
      required: true
      schema:
        type: string
        format: uuid

  schemas:

    RunCreateRequest:
      type: object
      required:
        - query
        - domain_pack
        - risk_class
      properties:
        query:
          type: string
          description: User question or task description
        domain_pack:
          type: string
          description: Domain Pack identifier
        pack_version:
          type: string
          description: Locked pack version
        schema_version:
          type: string
        risk_class:
          type: string
          enum: [LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL]
        time_horizon:
          type: object
          properties:
            start:
              type: string
              format: date
            end:
              type: string
              format: date
        retrieval_policy_override:
          type: object
          additionalProperties: false
        require_human_approval:
          type: boolean
          default: false

    Run:
      type: object
      properties:
        run_id:
          type: string
          format: uuid
        status:
          type: string
          enum: [PENDING, RUNNING, COMPLETED, REFUSED, FAILED]
        created_at:
          type: string
          format: date-time
        config_hash:
          type: string
        trust_budget:
          type: number
        risk_class:
          type: string

    RunStatus:
      type: object
      properties:
        run_id:
          type: string
        status:
          type: string
        progress:
          type: number
          minimum: 0
          maximum: 1
        current_stage:
          type: string

    RunResult:
      oneOf:
        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/SynthesisResult"
        - $ref: "#/components/schemas/RefusalResult"

    SynthesisResult:
      type: object
      required:
        - status
        - summary
        - claims
        - evidence_summary
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: [COMPLETED]
        summary:
          type: string
        claims:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Claim"
        disputed_claims:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/Claim"
        unknowns:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
        evidence_summary:
          type: object
          properties:
            total_evidence_objects:
              type: integer
            source_breakdown:
              type: object
              additionalProperties:
                type: integer

    RefusalResult:
      type: object
      required:
        - status
        - reasons
      properties:
        status:
          type: string
          enum: [REFUSED]
        reasons:
          type: array
          items:
            $ref: "#/components/schemas/RefusalReason"

    RefusalReason:
      type: object
      properties:
        code:
          type: string
          enum:
            - INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE
            - UNRESOLVED_CONFLICTS
            - LOW_SOURCE_QUALITY
            - TRUST_BUDGET_EXCEEDED
            - CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION
        message:
          type: string

    EvidenceObject:
      type: object
      properties:
        evidence_id:
          type: string
          format: uuid
        source_uri:
          type: string
        source_type:
          type: string
        modality:
          type: string
          enum: [text, table, image]
        location:
          type: object
        extraction_method:
          type: string
        extraction_confidence:
          type: number

    Claim:
      type: object
      properties:
        claim_id:
          type: string
        text:
          type: string
        entities:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
        evidence_ids:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
        confidence_label:
          type: string
          enum:
            - SUPPORTED
            - WEAKLY_SUPPORTED
            - CONFLICTED
            - INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE

    ArtifactManifest:
      type: object
      properties:
        retrieval_plan:
          type: string
        conflict_sets:
          type: string
        constraint_results:
          type: string
        logs:
          type: string

Design Notes (Important)
1. Refusal is a first-class API outcome

RunResult is a union type: COMPLETED or REFUSED.
Clients must handle refusal explicitly.

2. No probabilities, ever

The API never returns numeric confidence or forecasts.
Only ordinal confidence labels are allowed.

3. Immutable runs

Runs are created → executed → read-only

No mutation endpoints exist

All overrides must be declared at creation time

4. Safe-by-default

HIGH / CRITICAL risk classes are expected to require human approval outside this API

P-MARBLE surfaces data; governance systems decide actions

5. Clean separation from R-MARBLE

This API cannot:

trigger BN inference

modify schemas

auto-loop retrieval

self-tune prompts

Those belong strictly to research.

